					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-855594#post-2035291</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-855594/cavalcade-hub#post-2035291</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 20 May 2014 04:34:35 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Captain Cain</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1522769</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I don't like how character's full qualifications and attributes are forced in to meet the standards of Cavalcade in a lot of these. It's not a problem with the rules of Cavalcade, just poor writing by people who want to get on board. If you introduce a character poorly just to meet these criteria the story is still bad.</p> <p>The aspects of the character are introduced shoddily, through inorganic exposition in dialogue or narration. Their name, their background, their description, to be put on the character list, done in a way that makes the reading shit. It's because there's a more defined 'minimum' for Cavalcade stories (they need these characteristics of the personalities involved for the story to be posted), so the writers get those in without making that introduction good.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-855594#post-2023656</guid>
